39
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:29,200
Secondly, it's the misinterpretation of
technical analysis or misinterpretation of
a chart when you pull it up.

40
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:42,340
So, there's many, many scenarios that
we're going to go through in the
presentation where, when you look at
certain things in a chart, retail traders
often misinterpret what they're seeing.

41
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:48,020
And that means it becomes unuseful rather
than useful as a tool.

42
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:50,660
So, let's go to the presentation.

43
00:05:51,440 --> 00:05:54,480
Let's take the first step in gatekeeping
and look at technical analysis.

44
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:59,360
And I'll see you at the end of video 20
with a summary of technical analysis TA.

45
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:08,540
Okay, so let's move on to the stage of
gatekeeping.

46
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:15,880
So, let's assume now that you've got tons
and tons and tons of ideas.

47
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:18,280
You've got a world view.

48
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:21,060
You've got ideas in commodities,
currencies, rates.

49
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:24,860
You've got ideas in sectors, stocks.

50
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:27,640
What do you do next?

51
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:32,340
Obviously, everybody thinks their ideas
are brilliant.

52
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:37,980
No one shortlists a bunch of ideas because
they're all rubbish.

53
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:40,880
Everybody thinks their ideas are great.

54
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:43,060
So, what do you do next?

55
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:49,560
You've got to put a barrier between
yourself and your capital.

56
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:51,400
Your ideas and your capital.

57
00:06:53,800 --> 00:07:00,740
The idea of putting a barrier between your
ideas and your real money is to stop
yourself doing something stupid.

58
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:07,520
What was the most annoying thing of being
a trader that we discussed yesterday?

59
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,160
When you're right and you lose money.

60
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:18,800
So, you buy a stock at 100 because you
think it's a great idea.

61
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:23,900
You get stopped out at 92 and then it goes
to 400.

62
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:35,780
If you have processes that put a barrier
between your ideas and your capital,
you're less likely to do stupid things.

63
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:44,080
So, what we're trying to do is go through
these processes to time things in the best
way possible.

64
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:50,640
So, when things end up in our portfolio,
at least we've done the work.

65
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:52,160
And if we're wrong, we're just wrong.

66
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:58,700
It's better to be wrong and lose money
than lose money and be right.

67
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:01,940
Does that make sense?

68
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:06,320
So, what do we do?

69
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:14,020
We apply a screening process of technical
analysis, TA, and price action indicators.

70
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:21,560
If all the planets are aligned and all
those boxes are ticked,

71
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:28,480
then we can seriously consider committing
capital to this idea, to an idea.

72
00:08:31,080 --> 00:08:33,620
So, this is what we're going to cover now.

73
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,260
Technical analysis in this part of the
process.

74
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:43,500
And TA is just one part of the gatekeeping
process to stop yourself doing something
stupid.

75
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:51,920
First, don't confuse technical analysis
with a tool that generates ideas.

76
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:55,180
Retail traders are doing it in totally the
reverse.

77
00:08:56,460 --> 00:08:58,220
All the processes are now in reverse.

78
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:00,740
So, what professional traders do.

79
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:04,080
So, professional traders will start at the
top and work their way down,

80
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:08,120
then pull up the chart to see if the chart
agrees with what they think.

81
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:12,080
So, your fundamentals come first.

82
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:14,400
Your world view, your industry view, your
sector view.

83
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:17,700
Your stock view, you pull up the chart.

84
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:21,600
Not pull up the chart, take a position.

85
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:24,000
When it goes wrong, then work out why.

86
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:27,480
Then justify it.

87
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:29,940
Then get a world view.

88
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:31,520
And then put it in your pension.

89
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:32,480
And it goes to zero.

90
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,780
That's the reverse order of doing things.

91
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:43,380
So, don't confuse TA with a tool that
starts and generates you ideas.

92
00:09:44,540 --> 00:09:48,780
The vast majority of technical analysis
indicators react to the price.

93
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,740
They follow the price.

94
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:54,960
The price itself is the indicator that's
important.

95
00:09:57,420 --> 00:09:59,040
So, it doesn't give you trade ideas.

96
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:05,360
What it does is it gives you a pictorial
representation of what's happened in the
past.

97
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:13,440
I might give you some clues as to when you
can time your entry to the trade.

98
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:16,920
It's not useless.

99
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:18,540
It's quite useful.

100
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:25,400
And we'll go through some of the TA stuff
that you can look at to time positions a
bit better.

101
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:31,420
Try to think of it as a traffic light
system.

102
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:35,060
Where you've got your fundamental view on
something.

103
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:38,040
Where you think the world's going to go
up, for example.

104
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:40,620
You think a sector's going to go up.

105
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:42,020
You think a stock's going to go up.

106
00:10:42,260 --> 00:10:43,320
Then you pull up the chart.

107
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:49,660
And the chart literally says, there's no
way you should be buying this at the
moment.

108
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:56,420
It's a red in the traffic light system.

109
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:58,460
Just stick it on your watch list.

110
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:00,800
When the technicals move in your favour.

111
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:02,860
Then the timing is better.

112
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:07,780
If you pull up the chart.

113
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:10,840
And technically everything agrees with
what you're thinking.

114
00:11:11,760 --> 00:11:13,480
And it looks like a great entry point.

115
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:16,560
Don't be afraid to commit some capital to
