130
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:52,380
Give myself a chance of making money.

131
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:55,900
The contribution of that position to the
rest of your portfolio.

132
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:56,920
Your portfolio should not hurt you.

133
00:11:58,660 --> 00:11:59,500
In the short term.

134
00:12:03,220 --> 00:12:04,480
Big mistakes of TA.

135
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:06,140
First one we've covered.

136
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:08,580
Getting a trade idea from a chart.

137
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:10,260
It's totally amateur.

138
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:23,960
Going short of an asset that you're
fundamentally bullish on because the
technicals are bearish.

139
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:31,700
So you pull up the chart and the
technicals look like the stock is going
down.

140
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:36,460
But everything you've done up to this
point says that stock a year from now will
be higher.

141
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:41,140
And you get convinced by the chart to
short it.

142
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:42,960
And then it goes through the roof.

143
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:45,680
Vice versa.

144
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:49,060
Going long an asset that you're
fundamentally bearish on.

145
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:50,620
You pull up the chart.

146
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:56,520
It looks like technically everything's
great.

147
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:58,860
And it looks like it's going to go up
forever.

148
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:02,380
All the work to that point you've done is
bearish.

149
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:06,600
And you get convinced by the chart to buy
some.

150
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:08,600
And then it halves.

151
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:17,260
Again, no worse feeling in the world to
know the real situation, be right and use
money.

152
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:19,880
This happens time and time again.

153
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:21,880
Even in the professional world.

154
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:24,140
That's the type of stuff you get fired
for.

155
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:31,700
Where you walk into an office and ask for
an increase in capital because you've done
loads of work on the situation.

156
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:34,040
And you're fundamentally bullish on it.

157
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:38,220
And then the chart sucks you in to be
short.

158
00:13:38,220 --> 00:13:43,700
And then you end up losing money.

159
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:45,440
You'll get fired for it.

160
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:54,400
So before you pull up your charts, you're
going to have fundamental predispositions.

161
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:56,800
Now this is where you have to be careful.

162
00:13:58,980 --> 00:14:03,500
Because when you're fundamentally bullish
on something and the technicals aren't
quite there.

163
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:06,500
Or fundamentally bearish on something and
the technicals aren't quite there.

164
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:11,140
You're better not to participate at the
moment.

165
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:18,760
But when you've got fundamental
predispositions, it's very difficult to
control those emotions to stop yourself
doing stupid things.

166
00:14:21,140 --> 00:14:23,120
You have to just stick it on the watch
list and wait.

167
00:14:23,680 --> 00:14:24,260
And be patient.

168
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:26,820
Nothing wrong with being patient.

169
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:31,520
You can end up buying a stock higher than
where it was when you first started
looking at it.

170
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:34,260
But the technicals are all in your favour.

171
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:37,860
The risk reward on that trade is now
better.

172
00:14:44,100 --> 00:14:47,980
So in terms of technicals, you can get as
complicated as you want.

173
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:57,060
If you feel the need to get complicated on
technicals, and you know much more than me
about TA, which some of you probably will.

174
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:01,960
Feel free to add it into this section.

175
00:15:05,540 --> 00:15:06,940
But see it for what it is.

176
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:10,040
It's a chart.

177
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,860
And the chart follows the price.

178
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:17,280
All the technical indicators follow the
price.

179
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:18,940
The price is the most important.

180
00:15:22,220 --> 00:15:24,740
So you can add any amount of technicals
into this point.

181
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:26,860
Anywhere you want.

182
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:27,680
That's fine.

183
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:36,660
But make sure when you're looking at TA,
you treat it for what it is and put it in
the process at the right, where it
belongs.

184
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:38,740
Don't work backwards.

185
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:46,200
Start with technicals and then find out
fundamental reasons why you should be
doing something.

186
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:47,840
Because the chart is telling you to do
something.

187
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:58,800
So often technicals will tell you as much
as what not to do as to what to do.

188
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:06,620
So given your fundamental predisposition
of being bearish, do you short the stock
when you see this?

189
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:10,600
No, you wait for it to break.

190
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:20,320
If your fundamental predisposition is
bullish, this confirms what you think.

191
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:25,360
So you're now looking for entry around
trend, if you can get it.

192
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:31,480
Trending stocks downwards.

193
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:35,800
If your fundamental predisposition is
bullish, do you buy this?

194
00:16:36,660 --> 00:16:36,960
No.

195
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:37,740
No.

196
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:38,900
Stick it on the watch list.

197
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:41,260
Wait for it to break up to the upside.

198
00:16:41,860 --> 00:16:42,940
Wait for it to break the trend.

